 `feedback` is present for `annotated` decisions, and for `approved` decisions when the reviewer approved with notes (`--gate --json` only). Approval notes are non-blocking guidance — they are not a request for another revision.
 
+Local direct `--json` sessions detect tab closure without `--gate` or approval controls. After the last connected tab disconnects, a 30-second grace period permits reconnection. If no tab reconnects, the session returns `{"decision":"dismissed"}`. The CLI then waits 1.5 seconds before it stops the server and emits the result.
+
+This behavior excludes plaintext, hook, remote, shared, and tailnet-published sessions. A browser that never connects still requires caller-side cancellation. The grace period starts when the server detects disconnection, so half-open network failures can take longer.
+
 ### `--hook`
 
 Emits hook-native JSON that works directly with Claude Code and Codex PostToolUse/Stop hook protocols. Implies `--gate` (always three-button UX). Approve and Close emit empty stdout (hook passes), Send Annotations emits `{"decision":"block","reason":"<feedback>"}` (hook blocks with feedback).
